bc250: restore the CH7218's DSC decoder when its firmware denies it

Split out of ch7218-pcon-quirk, and unlike the rest of that patch this one
is always on when a CH7218 is present.

Some CH7218 firmware clears DP_DSC_SUPPORT while still returning a fully
populated DSC decoder capability block: a revision, slice capabilities and a
maximum bits-per-pixel, all describing a decoder the same block says is not
there. DC believes the bit, and since DP 1.4 HBR3 x4 cannot carry 4K120 RGB
uncompressed, the stream is rebuilt as YCbCr 4:2:2 10-bit. Nothing fails and
nothing is logged at any normal level -- the picture is simply worse.

Observed on an adapter that reports everything else correctly, so it is not
a property of the "broken" units the identity quirk exists for: DSC is
advertised at boot and selected (RGB 12-bpc, dsc:1), and after the display
had been in standby the next link bring-up re-read the capability block with
the bit clear and fell back to 4:2:2. Both standby cycles that day did it.

This is deliberately not behind amdgpu.bc250_ch7218_quirk. That parameter
guards a workaround that overrides what the adapter says about its
downstream port, which a healthy adapter reports correctly -- so it has to
be opt-in. This one cannot override a correct report at all: if DSC_SUPPORT
is set there is nothing to do, and if the capability block is empty the
adapter really has no decoder and is left alone. It only fires on the one
state that cannot be true, and then only re-states what the rest of the
block already says. amdgpu.bc250_hdmi21=0 switches it off with the rest of
the PCON path.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_capability.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_capability.c
index fad85a5..a7d082a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_capability.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_capability.c
@@ -1227,6 +1227,42 @@ static void bc250_ch7218_force_converter_identity(struct dc_link *link)
 	DC_LOG_DC("BC-250: CH7218 quirk: forced HDMI 2.1 FRL PCON identity, 48 Gbps\n");
 }
 
+/*
+ * Some CH7218 firmware clears DP_DSC_SUPPORT while still returning a fully
+ * populated DSC decoder capability block -- a combination that cannot describe
+ * real hardware, since a decoder that reports its revision, slice capabilities
+ * and maximum bits per pixel is a decoder that exists. Seen on an adapter that
+ * reports everything else correctly: DSC is advertised at boot, and the bit is
+ * gone after the display returns from standby, which silently drops 4K120 from
+ * RGB to YCbCr 4:2:2 on the next link bring-up.
+ *
+ * Unlike the identity quirk above this needs no module parameter, because it
+ * cannot reach an adapter that reports its DSC support truthfully: if the bit
+ * is set there is nothing to do, and if the capability block is empty the
+ * adapter really has no decoder and is left alone. Restoring the bit only
+ * re-states what the rest of the block already says. amdgpu.bc250_hdmi21=0
+ * switches it off along with the rest of the PCON path.
+ */
+static void bc250_ch7218_restore_dsc_support(struct dc_link *link)
+{
+	struct dpcd_dsc_capabilities *dsc_caps;
+
+	if (!bc250_ch7218_detected(link))
+		return;
+
+	dsc_caps = &link->dpcd_caps.dsc_caps;
+	if (dsc_caps->dsc_basic_caps.fields.dsc_support.DSC_SUPPORT)
+		return;
+
+	if (!dsc_caps->dsc_basic_caps.raw[DP_DSC_REV - DP_DSC_SUPPORT] &&
+	    !dsc_caps->dsc_basic_caps.raw[DP_DSC_SLICE_CAP_1 - DP_DSC_SUPPORT] &&
+	    !dsc_caps->dsc_basic_caps.raw[DP_DSC_MAX_BITS_PER_PIXEL_LOW - DP_DSC_SUPPORT])
+		return;
+
+	dsc_caps->dsc_basic_caps.fields.dsc_support.DSC_SUPPORT = true;
+	DC_LOG_DC("BC-250: CH7218: restored cleared DSC_SUPPORT\n");
+}
+
 static void get_active_converter_info(
 	uint8_t data, struct dc_link *link)
 {
@@ -2114,6 +2150,8 @@ static bool retrieve_link_cap(struct dc_link *link)
 				link->dpcd_caps.dsc_caps.dsc_basic_caps.raw,
 				sizeof(link->dpcd_caps.dsc_caps.dsc_basic_caps.raw));
 		if (status == DC_OK) {
+			/* BC-250: only acts on a CH7218 that contradicts itself. */
+			bc250_ch7218_restore_dsc_support(link);
 			is_fec_supported = link->dpcd_caps.fec_cap.bits.FEC_CAPABLE;
 			is_dsc_basic_supported = link->dpcd_caps.dsc_caps.dsc_basic_caps.fields.dsc_support.DSC_SUPPORT;
 			is_dsc_passthrough_supported = link->dpcd_caps.dsc_caps.dsc_basic_caps.fields.dsc_support.DSC_PASSTHROUGH_SUPPORT;
